      "date": "2026-04-05T23:43:21.000Z",
      "title": "Full year 2025 earnings: EPS misses analyst expectations",
      "body": "Full year 2025 results: EPS: ₹21.69 (up from ₹21.62 in FY 2024). Revenue: ₹94.1b (up 4.9% from FY 2024). Net income: ₹8.23b (flat on FY 2024). Profit margin: 8.7% (down from 9.2% in FY 2024). The decrease in margin was driven by higher expenses. Revenue was in line with analyst estimates. Earnings per share (EPS) missed analyst estimates by 2.7%. Revenue is forecast to grow 7.7% p.a. on average during the next 3 years, compared to a 11% growth forecast for the Auto Components industry in India. Over the last 3 years on average, earnings per share has increased by 2% per year whereas the company’s share price has increased by 7% per year.",
